    "text": "4 days ago\nS&P 500’s tech sector posts big drop as semiconductor stocks plunge\nThe S&P 500’s information-technology sector was posting a big drop on Friday, as semiconductor stocks were under intense selling pressure.\nTech was down 4.2%, making it the worst-performing sector of the S&P 500 by far, as the selloff eroded the sector’s outsize year-to-date gains of nearly 19%, according to FactSet.\n“Volatility is a two-edged sword,” said Jim Baird, chief investment officer at Plante Moran Financial Advisors, in an interview Friday. After outsize gains, stocks can periodically “take a step back, and it can come very quickly,” he said.",
